============================================================================
(bridge) H^2 - Pf^2 = 8Q  exhaustive: always a NON-NEG integer multiple of 8?
============================================================================
  n=4: all (H^2-Pf^2) divisible by 8: True; all >=0: True; Q in [0,3]; at max-H=5: |Pf|=1
  n=6: all (H^2-Pf^2) divisible by 8: True; all >=0: True; Q in [0,253]; at max-H=45: |Pf|=1
  => H=sqrt(Pf^2+8Q): the poly-time Pfaffian(det) is the SKELETON, Q the correction;
     Pf recurses n->n-2 (domino removal); H is #P-hard but pinned mod 8 by Pf (both odd).

DONE.
